WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.760
Good Morning John, I'm sorry about your face.

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:05.660
I wanted to make a video for you, uh, to make
you feel better, and I didn't know which kind

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:09.150
to make, so I asked Twitter if I should do
a rant video or a joke video.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.019
And man was it overwhelmingly in favor of
rants.

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:14.559
Why do you need to see me get angry instead
of be funny?!

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:19.130
Is the negative cognitive bias so prevalent
in our society, and in our brains, that we

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.560
can't just have a good time?

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.270
So, that was my first one.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.350
Let's talk about driving for a second.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.510
If you, uh, text while you're driving and
you say 'well it's okay, cause I'm really

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.050
good at it and I'm really careful.'

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.420
What you're really saying is: 'Well, I haven't
killed anyone...yet.'

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.420
Don't!

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:33.420
Don't!

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.750
Stop, just don't stop, believing.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:37.750
Where did I...what's happening?

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:41.640
This also goes for if you're waiting at a
light, especially if you're the first in line

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.250
and you're looking at your text message and
the light's green.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.640
Now in this situation, I will honk at you.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:52.520
This is not an excuse to get angry at me,
because you were the one not driving at a

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.520
green light!

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:59.559
I apologize for being so rude to you, I guess
I should have just sat there...forever...literally.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.550
Speaking of people who are incapable of not
looking at their phones every two seconds,

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:06.290
if that's you that's fine, but don't go to
movies.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:07.290
Just never do it.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:10.080
There's other ways to be entertained than
watching a movie while checking Facebook with

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.020
your brighter than the sun cellphone.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:16.080
Topic change: People who mock others for their
choice of major in school.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.850
Especially because it's almost always science
people, like myself, going after humanities

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:20.850
people.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.250
I'm sorry to bring this up, but interacting
with and creating for other humans is one

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.830
of the only things that computers are not
getting really, really good at really fast.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:30.659
So humanities jobs are actually pretty safe
from being automated away, so maybe don't

00:01:30.659 --> 00:01:31.659
be so entitled.

00:01:31.659 --> 00:01:36.980
Also people who mock others for using words
like "bae" or "boo" or "slay:" look, language

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:42.130
is fluid, and subcultures define themselves
by using slang terms; you do that too.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:44.740
What you're really saying when you complain
about other people's slang words is: 'my subculture

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:46.770
is better than yours.'

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:50.310
Which of course you do believe,;we all believe
that, but getting up on your soapbox and shouting

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.630
about it makes you look pretentious and patronizing.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.922
So, yeah, if your definition of rant is just
complaining about people who happen to be

00:01:55.922 --> 00:01:58.380
different from you: you're a big bag of farts.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.380
Do you run a website?

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.409
Are you thinking about requiring the users
of that website to do something?

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:07.100
Do not ask them if they would like to do that
thing if you're going to require it.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.619
Because if I"m asked, and I click 'no, I don't
want to do that.'

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:13.590
And then the website says 'okay, we'll ask
again later.'

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:15.180
That's not a good user experience!'

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.810
Like all cars have screens in them now.

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:19.209
I don't have a car like this but all the new
ones do.

00:02:19.209 --> 00:02:23.709
Here's what I've noticed, instead of using
the absolutely free and wonderful Android

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:27.870
operating system, car companies have insisted
on creating their own operating systems and

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:28.870
software.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.530
And the software is awful!

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:34.750
Congratulations on making a brand new car
feel like a first generation iPhone.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:38.200
The software is so unresponsive, you hit a
button and then it's like 'Oh, let me think

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.310
about that for a second.'

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:41.280
And then you're like, did you register that
I hit the button?'

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.430
So you hit it a few more times.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:45.600
And then the software is like 'Oh, let me
register all of those punches in sequence

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.440
on multiple screens as we go through.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:50.210
Even though you couldn't see these things
when you were hitting the buttons.'

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:52.600
And suddenly you've reached some obscure place
inside the software, and you've lowered your

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.300
dash lights in a way that you'll never be
able to figure out how to undo.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:59.400
Hey if somebody is like, "Please don't use
that word in that way; it makes me feel bad

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.400
about myself."

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.379
How about you don't get all defensive, and
start defending yourse--just don't use that

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:06.569
word in that way because it makes them feel
bad about themselves!

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:10.070
Now if you've ever talked about leveraging
online influencers to connect with digital

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:13.640
natives through mobile snack-able content,
you're fired.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:15.910
Just go to your desk, get your stuff, leave.

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:19.810
I went to school for like 85 years and no
one ever taught me how to do my taxes.

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:20.810
What?

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:21.810
What the?!

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:22.810
Why wouldn't you?!

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:26.670
School's paid for by the government, and they
want you to pay taxes.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.120
Why wouldn't they teach you that?

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.670
Also, I know how to do long division...why?

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:34.360
Why do I know how to solve a quadratic equation
without knowing what a quadratic equation

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:35.360
is?

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:36.360
Wha?

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.740
Maybe that should have been the time when
you were teaching me how to do my taxes.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.379
Also cursive writing, do they still do that?

00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:42.569
Because, ugh, I was so bad at it and I spent
so much of life learning how to do this thing

00:03:42.569 --> 00:03:43.569
that I've never done.

00:03:43.569 --> 00:03:47.660
And finally, my final rant of this rant video:
cable news.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.610
Ughhh.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:50.610
Thanks for watching John.

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:52.270
I hope you enjoyed it and I'll see you on
Tuesday.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:55.790
You can watch my first rant video over there,
also the giraffe love design is back except

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:58.709
with better colors - it's shiny, and we got
new tank tops for summer.

